  "translation": "On Sunday, our whole family went together to a park on the outskirts. The facilities in the park were all available. We set out from home and arrived after half an hour's drive. Inside the park, flowers and grass were lush and the scenery was very beautiful. Mom really likes flowers, so she often looked east and west, taking many photos. There is also a lake in the park; Dad and I took a walk by the lake. Suddenly, I heard a bird call. I looked up and saw a small bird fall from a tree. This little bird was motionless, without strength, seemingly injured. I asked Dad: 'How can we save it?' Dad said: 'First feed it a few mouthfuls of water.' I immediately ran over and gently picked it up. When I got home, I fed it a piece of bread. It ate it all up. The next day, it completely recovered its spirit. We set it free to fly back into the blue sky, and it could fly."
